00:17:33,790 --> 00:17:45,130
And those things are very dangerous to post-train the model on because the way, just to like take a step back and talk about training, there's pre-training where we are just taking a lot of data and showing to the model.

198
00:17:45,890 --> 00:17:52,190
Then there's mid-training and post-training where increasingly models become aligned to the tasks that they will do in the real world.

199
00:17:52,870 --> 00:18:06,170
And if you show the models the task that are misaligned, for instance, that have these templates in it or synthetically generated, but are not high quality, then the models, you do the whole training run.

